// v24 Aim convergence (docs/aim-convergence-v24.md). A ship that holds its fire settles its aim; every volley it fires
// throws it off again. aim runs 0 (just fired, widest) to 1 (fully settled); the shot spread is scaled by
// aimSpread(aim), from `wide` down to `tight`. The aim settles at a rate set by the fire-control capacity for the
// guns it serves: aimRatio is the fire-control compartments' volume over volumePerGun m³ for each gun (an Imperial
// is about 1), or a craft's targeting capacity over its demand; the rate is baseRate × √ratio within the limits.
// Manoeuvring throws the aim off too: motion is the turn rate over the ship's own maximum plus 0.7 × the
// acceleration (speeding up or braking) over its own maximum (at most 1.5); the aim loses motionK × motion per second.
