// ---------- v22 ordnance as stores ----------
// Each round is a physical object: a length and diameter (m), a mass (t) and what its hit delivers (TT; an ion
// round's TT enter shield acceptance and connected-grid overload). Rounds ride in the craft's store stations —
// a launch tube's magazine, the bomb bay, a wing pylon — and are used up as they are fired; the craft rearms in
// its carrier's hangar. The designer shows only what the stations can take; the order of battle chooses what
// each squadron carries (お任せ: the craft's canon loadout, CRAFT_LOADOUT).
// Sizes and masses: neither canon nor Legends gives figures for the rounds, so they are the game's, sized to the
// launchers measured on the examples (a proton torpedo fills the 1.4 m × 0.5 m tube box of the X-wing's MG7).
// Hits: the game's, set so a canon loadout's first attack run comes out near the voyage craft table's strike
// (an X-wing's two torpedoes and guns about 160, a TIE/sa's torpedoes and bombs about 380, a Y-wing's about 300).
// v30 The size and yield of rounds (ordnance specification, and user decisions 2026-11-18/19「対艦魚雷は7×50をベースに」「航空魚雷は1×2
// サイズで、95%が弾頭。ミサイル、爆弾も同じサイズ」). A round's mass is its body's volume at ORDNANCE_BASIS.density; its yield is its
// warhead's mass at .warheadTTPerT. The figures of that first version (36.56 TT; one air round of 0.0597 TT for torpedo, missile
// and bomb alike) are replaced by those given with AIR_ROUNDS below, and the table ORDNANCE below takes them (2026-11-19).
const ORDNANCE_BASIS=Object.freeze({density:1,warheadTTPerT:.03/* user decision 2026-11-19「係数は0.03」: was .02. The whole of a tonne as energy (E=mc²) is 0.0215 TT, so .03 is 1.4 times that: a figure of the game, not of physics */});
function ordnanceBody(D,L,warheadFraction,ball){const mass=ORDNANCE_BASIS.density*(ball?Math.PI/6*D*D*D/* a sphere of diameter D */:Math.PI/4*D*D*L),warheadMass=mass*warheadFraction;return {dims:[L,D],mass,warheadFraction,warheadMass,tt:warheadMass*ORDNANCE_BASIS.warheadTTPerT};}
// 2026-11-27 Designed rounds (docs/missile-design-spec-2026-11-27.md). User decisions「ミサイル魚雷は『弾頭部』『推進剤』『弾芯』に分ける」
// 「弾芯は無しから鉄〜タングステンくらいまで密度を変えることができ、それに従い重量が増える。密度は貫通力に繋がる」「ミサイル全体質量の5%の推進剤は
// 誘導制御、姿勢制御に使われる」「配分は自由に決める」「推進剤の性能は今の魚雷(95:5)の追尾能力に同じ」「魚雷は速度よりも速度を維持する方向に推進剤を
// 使う」「推進剤の中で制御用と加速用で分ける」, and the reading confirmed「その理解で進める」: a round's body (diameter D, length L) is shared by
// volume between its warhead, its control propellant, its main (accel) propellant and its core. The control propellant is at least
// ROUND_DESIGN.controlMin of the round's whole mass; its share sets the round's lateral acceleration (ROUND_DESIGN.latPer5 for each 5%),
// and it is spent as the round turns. The main propellant either speeds the round up ('accel') or holds its launch speed against what
